    "PREAMBLE": "Sangeeta Rani And Ors vs State Of Haryana And Others on 19\nMay, 2023\nNeutral Citation No:=2023\nCrm-M-13950-2023 2023:Phhc:073673 \n In The High Court Of Punjab And Haryana\n At Chandigarh\nSr. No.237 Crm-M-13950-2023\nDate of decision: May 19th, 202\nSangeeta Rani And Ors ...........Peti\n versus\nState Of Haryana And Others .......Respond\nCoram: Hon'Ble Mr. Justice Namit Kumar\nPresent: Mr. Rahul Bhargava, Advocate\n for the petitioners.\nMr. Zorawar Singh Chauhan, Dag, Haryana.\nNamit Kumar, J. (Oral)\nDuring enquiry, he had produced 2 of 3 Neutral Citation No:=2023:PHHC:073673 the receipt of Rs. 40,000/- dated 03.07.2022 given to accused Yashpal, Rs. 6000/- dated 17.07.2022 given to accused Neeraj Gupta, Rs. 8000 dated 23.07.2022 and Rs. 16,000/- given to accused Lakshay Singhal through Google Pay and Phone pay.\nThe copy of receipt were taken into the police possession by the Investigating Officer vide memo.\nxxx xxx xxx xxx\"\nSangeeta Rani And Ors vs State Of Haryana And Others on 19 May, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/103086826/\n2\nSince the statements of the petitioners have been recorded by the Investigating Officer, as claimed in the present petition, therefore, the instant petition has been rendered infructuous and the same is disposed of accordingly.\n(NAMIT KUMAR)\n",
    "facts": "The instant petition has been filed by the petitioners under Section 482 of Code of Criminal Procedure seeking directions to respondent Nos.2 and 3 to comply with the mandatory provisions of law, as envisaged under Section 154(1) of Code of Criminal Procedure and subsequently record the statements of the petitioners in case FIR No.706 dated 28.08.2022, under Sections 406, 420, 467,\n468, 474, 477, 199, 200, 506 and 120 of IPC, registered at Police Station Indri, District Karnal (Annexure P-1).\nThat on 31.03.2023 & 03.05.2023, petitioner Sangeeta Rani D/o Somnath was joined in the investigation before the Investigating Officer and he had produced bank statement of her account bearing No. 50200036975849 HDFC Bank from Sangeeta Rani And Ors vs State Of Haryana And Others on 19 May, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/103086826/\n1 01.06.2022 to 31.07.2022 to ASI Bahadur Singh and same was taken into the police possession vide memo and statement of victim/ petitioner was also recorded by the 1 of 3 Neutral Citation No:=2023:PHHC:073673 Investigating Officer under section 161 Cr.P.C,\nin which she alleged that she had given Rs. 50,000/- to Lakshay Singhal on 21.07.2022, Rs. 3,000/- on 21.07.2022, Rs. 50,000/- to accused Paras on 19.07.2022, Rs. 40,000/- to Divanshu on 20.07.2022 and in this regard she had over a copy of UPI transactions showing transfer of Rs. 1,43,000/- from the bank account of Sangeet Rani.\nRs. 2,40,000/- Ashu (investor), Rs. 27,000/- of Reenu, Rs. 40,000/- of Vinay in cash had given to Lakshay and Anil Singhal through Sangeet Rani (petitioner No. 1).\nThereafter, on 04.05.2023, another victim namely Vipin Kumar S/o Rajbir R/o Village Budhedi, Police Station Indri, District Karnal (petitioner No. 3) was joined in the investigation and his statement under section 161 of Cr.P.C. was recorded separately.\nDuring investigation, he had produced the receipt of Phone Pay app of Rs. 8000/- on 11.07.2022 and Rs. 88000/- dated 22.07.2022,\nwhich were given by him to accused Lakshay and Neeraj Rani and copy of receipt were taken into the police possession vide memo.\nOn the same day, victim Balbir Singh S/o Rulda Ram R/o Bibipur Jattan Police Station Indri, Karnal (petitioner No.\n2) was joined in the investigation and his statement under section 161 of Cr.P.C. was recorded by the Investigating Officer.\n"
